NAIJACLIPS v0.2 — GLOBAL CREATOR PLATFORM FOUNDATION

This package contains the existing mobile-first browser prototype plus a starter Supabase database schema for the next multi-user milestone.

WHAT IS INCLUDED
- index.html: existing front-end preview (local-device prototype)
- manifest.json: web app manifest
- supabase/schema.sql: starter database schema and row-level security policies for profiles, videos, likes, comments, follows, and content reports

IMPORTANT: THIS IS NOT YET A LIVE MULTI-USER APP
The existing index.html still stores user-uploaded video files in the current browser/device. The SQL is a backend foundation, not a connected backend. No Supabase project credentials, cloud storage upload flow, real login UI, transcoding, moderation console, ads, payment processing, or creator payouts are included/active in this package. Do not claim creators can earn money yet.

NEXT SETUP STEPS
1. Create a Supabase project at https://supabase.com/dashboard.
2. In Supabase SQL Editor, review and run supabase/schema.sql.
3. In Storage, create a bucket named naijaclips-videos. For a public MVP, only allow public playback of published content and restrict uploads/updates/deletes to authenticated users' own folder. Set a sensible file-size limit and allow only supported video MIME types. A private bucket with signed URLs is preferable for private/unlisted videos.
4. Add Storage policies for bucket_id = 'naijaclips-videos'. For authenticated upload/update/delete, require the first folder in the object path to equal auth.uid()::text. Do not let users overwrite another user's path. Public read should be enabled only if the bucket is intended for public videos.
5. Connect the front end using the Supabase project URL and anon/publishable key. It is safe to use the publishable/anon key in a browser only when Row Level Security and policies are configured correctly. NEVER place a service_role/secret key in index.html or any public file.
6. Implement email verification, account creation, profile creation, cloud upload, feed pagination, likes/comments/follows, account deletion, and reporting before inviting the public.
7. Add server-side checks, upload size/duration limits, malware/content scanning where practical, copyright reporting/takedown, moderation review, privacy policy, terms, age-appropriate safeguards, and backups.
8. Only after the product has real users and legal/provider approval should advertising and creator payouts be integrated. Track earnings server-side; never trust client-submitted view counts or balance values.

DEPLOY FRONT-END PREVIEW
- Extract the ZIP.
- Upload the front-end files to Netlify Drop: https://app.netlify.com/drop
- This publishes a preview only; it does not connect the database or make uploads shared.

BUILD STATUS
This is a development starter, not a production-ready social network. Test on iPhone and Android, and perform a security review before public launch.
