# NaijaClips cloud backend setup (Supabase)

This starter adds an optional shared public feed and email/password accounts. It requires you to create and configure your own Supabase project; no account, project key, storage, or paid plan is included.

## 1. Create the backend
1. Create a project at https://supabase.com/ and keep its database password private.
2. In the Supabase SQL Editor, run `backend/supabase-schema.sql` from this ZIP.
3. Open Project Settings → API and copy the Project URL and the public anon/publishable key.
4. Edit `supabase-config.js` and replace both placeholders. Only use the public anon/publishable key in the website. Never expose a `service_role` or secret key.
5. Deploy the whole folder to Netlify. `index.html`, `supabase-config.js`, `cloud.js`, `manifest.webmanifest`, `sw.js`, and `icons/` must be at the site root.

## 2. Enable account email confirmation
In Supabase Authentication settings, configure the site's Site URL and redirect URLs to your exact HTTPS Netlify domain. Decide whether to require email confirmation before public posting. Test sign-up, sign-in, sign-out, posting, playback and deletion using two different accounts/devices.

## 3. What the cloud starter does
- Creates email/password accounts through Supabase Auth.
- Uploads video files to Supabase Storage (up to 250 MB per file in this starter).
- Stores public clip metadata in Postgres and lists it in a shared feed.
- Allows authenticated users to delete only their own clips, using row-level security.
- Public clips can be watched by visitors; posting requires sign-in.

The existing local-device prototype is retained. The cloud panel works only after configuration. Do not publish with the placeholder configuration and expect cloud features to work.

## 4. Before a real public launch
This is an MVP backend scaffold, not a production-scale video service. Add automated video transcoding and adaptive streaming/CDN, rate limits and quotas, upload scanning, reporting/blocking/moderation, copyright/takedown process, account recovery, privacy policy/terms, data export/deletion, backups, monitoring, abuse prevention and security review. Public storage can incur costs and exposes posted clips to anyone with their URLs. Establish budget alerts and quotas first.

## 5. Monetization reality
No revenue or creator payouts are enabled by this code. Ad networks, sponsors, analytics consent, eligibility rules, fraud checks, tax/compliance review and a payment/payout provider need separate integration. Never promise users guaranteed earnings based only on views.
# NaijaClips payout + community safety setup

This is implementation scaffolding, not a live payment account or a guarantee of approval. Start with Paystack test mode and never enable live transfers until the complete flow has been reviewed and tested.

## Database migration order
1. Run `supabase-schema.sql`.
2. Run `monetization.sql`.
3. Run `community-safety.sql`.
4. Run `payout-balance-fix.sql` (important: includes paid payouts in balance deductions and serializes requests per creator).

Review SQL and test row-level security using at least two ordinary user accounts before any public launch. The public clips policy now exposes only rows whose `moderation_status` is `published`. Admin moderation updates must happen only in a trusted server environment using the service-role key.

## Edge Functions
Deploy these Supabase Edge Functions:
- `admin-approve-payout`: admin-only approve/reject; does not transfer money.
- `admin-process-payout`: submits an approved payout to Paystack and leaves it `processing` until a signed webhook confirms outcome.
- `paystack-webhook`: verifies the `x-paystack-signature` HMAC and updates the matching processing payout.

Configure Edge Function secrets in Supabase, not in Netlify/browser JavaScript:
- `SUPABASE_URL`
- `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`
- `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` (secret; never share or put in frontend code)
- `PAYOUT_ADMIN_USER_IDS` (comma-separated Supabase Auth user UUIDs that are trusted payout admins)
- `PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY` (start with Paystack test secret key)
- `APP_ORIGIN` (the exact HTTPS origin of the deployed NaijaClips site)

Register the deployed `paystack-webhook` function URL in the Paystack dashboard as the transfer webhook endpoint. Confirm the event signature and transfer lifecycle using provider test mode. Never mark a payout paid from a browser response; only a verified provider event may do that. If a provider call times out or recipient creation fails, the request is deliberately left `processing` for human reconciliation to avoid accidental duplicate transfers. Do not retry until the provider dashboard confirms whether a transfer exists.

### Payout operations
1. Creator must have a saved payout profile and confirmed ledger earnings. Minimum request is ₦5,000.
2. A trusted admin reviews KYC, suspicious traffic, bank details, balance, applicable fees/taxes, and request history.
3. Admin calls `admin-approve-payout` with `{ "payoutRequestId": "UUID", "decision": "approve" }` or `reject`.
4. For an approved request only, an authenticated allowlisted admin may call `admin-process-payout` with `{ "payoutRequestId": "UUID" }`.
5. Wait for verified webhook; reconcile Paystack and database status. Keep audit evidence.

The code is a starter and needs a professional security review, test-mode end-to-end tests, idempotency/retry testing, operational alerts and legal/compliance review before live money is used. Do not publish a promise of guaranteed creator income.

## Reports and moderation
Authenticated users can submit reports via `content_reports`; they can read only their own submitted reports. Users can manage their own block list. There is no client policy allowing reports to be edited or dismissed. Build a staff-only moderation UI or use an authenticated admin Edge Function before public launch. Set clips to `hidden` or `removed` for moderation actions; only `published` clips are publicly readable.

## Must still be supplied by the owner
- Real Supabase project URL/public key and configured storage/auth redirects.
- Paystack business onboarding and API credentials, verified bank recipient handling, and admin UUIDs.
- Real support email, privacy/terms review, creator eligibility and payout rules.
- App Store Connect and Google Play developer accounts, app screenshots, signing certificates and platform-specific builds.
import { createClient } from 'https://esm.sh/@supabase/supabase-js@2';

const config = window.NAIJACLIPS_SUPABASE || {};
const $ = (id) => document.getElementById(id);
const ready = typeof config.url === 'string' && config.url.startsWith('https://') &&
  !config.url.includes('YOUR-PROJECT') && typeof config.anonKey === 'string' &&
  config.anonKey.length > 20 && !config.anonKey.includes('YOUR_SUPABASE');
const cloudStatus = $('cloudStatus');
const cloudFeed = $('cloudFeed');
let supabase = null;
let currentUser = null;

function status(message, error = false) {
  cloudStatus.textContent = message;
  cloudStatus.style.color = error ? '#ff9b9b' : 'var(--green)';
}
function escapeHtml(value) {
  return String(value ?? '').replace(/[&<>"']/g, c => ({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]));
}
function humanSize(bytes) {
  return bytes >= 1048576 ? `${(bytes / 1048576).toFixed(1)} MB` : `${Math.max(1, Math.round(bytes / 1024))} KB`;
}
function publicVideoUrl(path) {
  return supabase.storage.from('clips').getPublicUrl(path).data.publicUrl;
}
function setSignedInUI(user) {
  currentUser = user || null;
  $('cloudAuthForm').classList.toggle('hidden', !!user);
  $('cloudSignOutAlt').classList.toggle('hidden', !user);
  $('cloudUploadForm').classList.toggle('hidden', !user);
  $('cloudUser').textContent = user ? `Signed in: ${user.email || 'account'}` : 'Not signed in';
}
function renderCloudCards(clips) {
  if (!clips.length) {
    cloudFeed.innerHTML = '<div class="empty-state"><div style="font-size:2rem">🌍</div><h3>No public clips yet</h3><p>When someone posts a cloud clip, it can appear here for other visitors too.</p></div>';
    return;
  }
  cloudFeed.innerHTML = '';
  for (const clip of clips) {
    const card = document.createElement('article');
    card.className = 'card';
    const url = publicVideoUrl(clip.storage_path);
    card.innerHTML = `<div class="video-wrap"><video controls playsinline preload="metadata" src="${escapeHtml(url)}" aria-label="${escapeHtml(clip.caption)}"></video></div><div class="card-body"><div class="caption">${escapeHtml(clip.caption)}</div><div class="meta"><span>${new Date(clip.created_at).toLocaleDateString()}</span><span>${humanSize(clip.size_bytes)}</span></div><div class="card-actions"><button data-download>↓ Download</button><button class="secondary" data-share>↗ Share</button>${currentUser && currentUser.id !== clip.user_id ? '<button class="secondary" data-report>⚑ Report</button>' : ''}${currentUser && currentUser.id === clip.user_id ? '<button class="danger" data-delete>Delete</button>' : ''}</div></div>`;
    card.querySelector('[data-download]').addEventListener('click', () => {
      const a = document.createElement('a'); a.href = url; a.download = clip.original_filename || 'naijaclips-video.mp4'; a.target = '_blank'; a.rel = 'noopener'; document.body.appendChild(a); a.click(); a.remove();
    });
    card.querySelector('[data-share]').addEventListener('click', async () => {
      try {
        if (navigator.share) await navigator.share({title:'NaijaClips', text:clip.caption, url});
        else { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(url); status('Video link copied.'); }
      } catch (e) { if (e?.name !== 'AbortError') status('Could not share this link.', true); }
    });
    const report = card.querySelector('[data-report]');
    if (report) report.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      if (!currentUser) { status('Sign in before reporting a clip.', true); return; }
      const choices = 'nudity, violence, hate, harassment, spam, copyright, underage_safety, other';
      const reason = prompt(`Why are you reporting this clip? Enter one reason exactly:\n${choices}`, 'spam');
      if (!reason) return;
      const normalized = reason.trim().toLowerCase();
      if (!choices.split(', ').includes(normalized)) { status('Please enter one of the listed report reasons.', true); return; }
      const details = prompt('Optional details (max 1000 characters):', '') || '';
      report.disabled = true;
      const { error } = await supabase.from('content_reports').insert({
        reporter_user_id: currentUser.id, clip_id: clip.id, reported_user_id: clip.user_id,
        reason: normalized, details: details.slice(0, 1000)
      });
      report.disabled = false;
      if (error) { status('Report could not be submitted. Apply backend/community-safety.sql first. ' + error.message, true); return; }
      status('Report submitted. Our moderation process still needs an operator to review it.');
    });
    const del = card.querySelector('[data-delete]');
    if (del) del.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      if (!confirm('Delete this public clip? This removes the clip from the shared feed.')) return;
      del.disabled = true;
      const { error: storageError } = await supabase.storage.from('clips').remove([clip.storage_path]);
      if (storageError) { status(storageError.message, true); del.disabled = false; return; }
      const { error } = await supabase.from('clips').delete().eq('id', clip.id).eq('user_id', currentUser.id);
      if (error) { status(error.message, true); return; }
      status('Your clip was deleted.'); await loadCloudFeed();
    });
    cloudFeed.appendChild(card);
  }
}
async function loadCloudFeed() {
  if (!supabase) return;
  cloudFeed.innerHTML = '<div class="empty-state">Loading shared clips…</div>';
  const { data, error } = await supabase.from('clips').select('id,user_id,caption,storage_path,original_filename,content_type,size_bytes,created_at').order('created_at', {ascending:false}).limit(60);
  if (error) { cloudFeed.innerHTML = '<div class="empty-state">Could not load cloud feed. Check the setup guide and Supabase policies.</div>'; status(error.message, true); return; }
  renderCloudCards(data || []);
  $('cloudCount').textContent = String((data || []).length);
}
async function init() {
  if (!ready) {
    status('Cloud mode is not configured yet. Add your Supabase URL and public anon/publishable key in supabase-config.js.', true);
    cloudFeed.innerHTML = '<div class="empty-state"><div style="font-size:2rem">☁️</div><h3>Cloud feed setup needed</h3><p>Follow backend/CLOUD_SETUP.md. Until then, use the local-device feed below.</p></div>';
    $('cloudAuthForm').classList.remove('hidden'); $('cloudUploadForm').classList.add('hidden'); $('cloudAuthForm').querySelectorAll('input,button').forEach(el => el.disabled = true);
    return;
  }
  supabase = createClient(config.url, config.anonKey, {auth:{persistSession:true,autoRefreshToken:true,detectSessionInUrl:true}});
  const { data: { session } } = await supabase.auth.getSession();
  setSignedInUI(session?.user);
  supabase.auth.onAuthStateChange((_event, sessionNow) => { setSignedInUI(sessionNow?.user); loadCloudFeed(); });
  await loadCloudFeed();
}
$('cloudAuthForm').addEventListener('submit', async (event) => {
  event.preventDefault(); if (!supabase) return;
  const email = $('cloudEmail').value.trim(); const password = $('cloudPassword').value;
  const action = event.submitter?.dataset.authAction || 'signin';
  status(action === 'signup' ? 'Creating account…' : 'Signing in…');
  const result = action === 'signup'
    ? await supabase.auth.signUp({email, password})
    : await supabase.auth.signInWithPassword({email, password});
  if (result.error) { status(result.error.message, true); return; }
  if (action === 'signup' && !result.data.session) status('Account created. Check your email to confirm it, then sign in.');
  else { setSignedInUI(result.data.user); status('You are signed in.'); await loadCloudFeed(); }
});
$('cloudSignOutAlt').addEventListener('click', async () => { if (!supabase) return; const {error} = await supabase.auth.signOut(); if (error) status(error.message, true); else {setSignedInUI(null); status('Signed out.'); await loadCloudFeed();} });
$('cloudUploadForm').addEventListener('submit', async (event) => {
  event.preventDefault();
  if (!supabase || !currentUser) { status('Sign in before posting.', true); return; }
  const file = $('cloudVideoFile').files[0]; const caption = $('cloudCaption').value.trim();
  if (!file || !caption) return;
  if (!file.type.startsWith('video/')) { status('Please choose a video file.', true); return; }
  if (file.size > 250 * 1024 * 1024) { status('The current upload limit is 250 MB.', true); return; }
  const btn = $('cloudPublishBtn'); btn.disabled = true; status('Uploading video to cloud storage…');
  const ext = (file.name.split('.').pop() || 'mp4').toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]/g, '') || 'mp4';
  const path = `${currentUser.id}/${crypto.randomUUID()}.${ext}`;
  const { error: uploadError } = await supabase.storage.from('clips').upload(path, file, {contentType:file.type, upsert:false});
  if (uploadError) { status(uploadError.message, true); btn.disabled = false; return; }
  const { error: insertError } = await supabase.from('clips').insert({user_id:currentUser.id,caption,storage_path:path,original_filename:file.name,content_type:file.type,size_bytes:file.size});
  if (insertError) {
    await supabase.storage.from('clips').remove([path]);
    status(insertError.message, true); btn.disabled = false; return;
  }
  $('cloudUploadForm').reset(); status('Published to the shared cloud feed.'); await loadCloudFeed(); btn.disabled = false;
});
init().catch(error => { console.error(error); status('Cloud setup error: ' + (error.message || 'unknown error'), true); });
